{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "So Much to Do at Work", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Big Trouble, Huge Trouble", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Discuss factual and abstract information about common everyday or job related topics in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "disastrous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "terrible; bad; unsuccessful ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It was as disastrous as that time you had me help you with that art assignment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about a problem. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "running low on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to near the end of a supply of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was running low on gas! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "notepad", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of sheets of paper fastened together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I realized my notepad was nowhere to be found.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tardiness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of arriving late", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I apologized for my tardiness.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to extend", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stretch out your hand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I extended my hand out for a handshake.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to knock over", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hit something with a short quick action so that it falls", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I knocked over a mug and spilt coffee all over the carpet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to vanish", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to disappear ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My notes had vanished!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to copy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at someone else's work and write the same thing as they have", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I copied her notes. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Infinitives in the Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You form the passive infinitive of verbs by putting<span class=\"italic\"> to be</span> in front of the<span class=\"italic\"> past participle</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Look at the chart for a comparison of active and passive forms of the infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Active\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Passive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There's so much <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to do</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There's so much <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to be done</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm going <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to do</span> it by Friday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It's going <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to be done</span> by Friday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I had <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to fill up</span> the tank.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The tank had <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to be filled up</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I had <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to find</span> my notepad!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My notepad was nowhere <span <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to be found</span> and I needed it! \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He needs <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to clean</span> the carpet.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">That carpet definitely needs <span class=\\\"strong\\\">to be cleaned</span>. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Causative - <span class=\"italic\">get/have</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use a causative verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. The subject caused the action to happen.  They didn't do it themselves. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"italic\">get/have</span> when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. <br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>   <span class=\"italic\">Have your spouse or housemates clean up after themselves.</span> <br/><br/>  In this sentence you ask or persuade your spouse to clean up after themselves.<br/><br/>  The structure of the causative is:<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> have</span> + object + verb<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Have someone remind</span> everyone.</span><br/><br/> Or:   subject +<span class=\"italic\"> get </span>+ object + Infinitive <br/><br/>   <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Get everyone to choose</span> their favorite music to play.</span><br/><br/>  Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get</span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You had me help you with that art assignment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had the attendant pump my gas. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I got Mr. Brody to give me an extra day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I got her to lend me her laptop.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a time where something misfortunate happened to you at school or at work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell a partner about what happened. What did someone else do for you to help you?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your friend about something that's happened to them.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about a misfortunate event that has happened to me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain how I solved a problem.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain how someone helped me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask a friend about a misfortunate event that happened to them.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id":